        rdfs:label        "has quantile"@en , "Used to define a quantile for example on a data point of a quantile time series. The quantile must be a ratio, usually a percentage. In a quantile forecast the hasQuantile property cannot be empty. his property assigns to the data point the percentage of values that are below this value. In other words, a data point with quantile 90 indicates that 90 % of other measurements are (estimated to be) lower. "@en ;
        sh:datatype       xsd:decimal ;
        sh:description    "Used to define a quantile for example on a data point of a quantile time series. The quantile must be a ratio, usually a percentage. In a quantile forecast the hasQuantile property cannot be empty. his property assigns to the data point the percentage of values that are below this value. In other words, a data point with quantile 90 indicates that 90 % of other measurements are (estimated to be) lower. "@en ;
        sh:name           "has quantile"@en ;
        sh:nodeKind       sh:Literal ;
        sh:path           s4ener:hasQuantile ;
        sh:pattern        "(\\+|-)?([0-9]+(\\.[0-9]*)?|\\.[0-9]+)" .

